---
type: agent/instruction
description: Hand an existing linked worktree to a fresh agent session
usage: "guide://_worktree/use/<worktree-name>"
minargs: 1
requires-handoff-context: true
requires-worktree-support: true
includes:
  - ../_partials/handoff-context-target
---
Using the current Git worktree inventory, read {{>handoff-context-target}}.
Locate the `worktrees.{{args.0.value}}` entry. It must exist, and its recorded
absolute `path` must appear in the fresh Git worktree inventory. If either check
fails, do not allocate a replacement name or hand off a child; refresh or repair
the handoff entry first. Use the recorded path, task metadata, phase, plan, and
instructions as the child handoff. Do not alter unrelated top-level entries or
worktree entries.

Give the child the worktree name `{{args.0.value}}`, its absolute recorded path,
and the complete handoff entry. Do not forward this session ID. The child must
work from that path, create a fresh Guide interaction, bind the shared project
root and that worktree, submit its local workflow file, then read the shared
handoff context before proceeding. The local workflow file is authoritative for
the label; if it is absent or unlabelled, add `worktree: {{args.0.value}}` while
preserving the workflow state before submitting it.
